WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.550
Last term our duty rota had the highest

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.870
total happiness in the staff room.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.970
And Salma got the duty she hates

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.970
most, every single week.

5
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.060
Was that really the best rota?

6
00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.310
Today: fairness by design, built into

7
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.570
the model, not added at the end.

8
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.260
There’s more than one way to

9
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.660
score a plan for a group.

10
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.710
The total adds up everyone’s score.

11
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.800
The worst-off looks only at

12
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.820
the person doing worst.

13
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.770
And the gap is the distance between

14
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.970
the best-off and the worst-off.

15
00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.730
Three teachers rate three duties from

16
00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.210
one to nine: the morning gate, the

17
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.770
lunch hall and the library.

18
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.840
The plan with the best total gives Amina

19
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.080
the gate, Joseph the lunch hall and Salma

20
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.960
the library: nineteen points.

21
00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:56.310
But Salma rates the library a two.

22
00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.120
Now change the goal: make the

23
00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.600
worst-off as well off as possible.

24
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.900
Amina takes the library, Joseph the

25
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.000
gate and Salma the lunch hall.

26
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.820
The total drops to eighteen, but

27
00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.400
nobody scores below five.

28
00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.390
The difference, one point here, is the

29
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.150
price of fairness: what the total gives

30
00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.150
up so the worst-off does better.

31
00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:22.890
Often it’s small.

32
00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.650
Sometimes it’s large, and then people must

33
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.570
decide together whether to pay it.

34
00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.000
In a model, fairness is

35
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.280
just a few more lines.

36
00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:36.990
Add a variable for the worst score.

37
00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.790
Say every teacher’s score is at

38
00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.290
least that, and maximise it.

39
00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:43.900
Quick check!

40
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.980
Two rotas both give the worst-off

41
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.300
teacher five, the best floor there is.

42
00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:52.970
How should the solver choose between them?

43
00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.820
Keep the floor of five, then make

44
00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.900
the total as big as possible.

45
00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.560
Solvers do it in two steps.

46
00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:05.240
Solve for the best floor, fix it as a

47
00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.540
limit, and solve again for the total.

48
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.550
Which rule is fair isn’t for the

49
00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:12.950
modeller alone to decide.

50
00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.360
Ask the people affected which measure they

51
00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.980
want, before anyone sees the result.

52
00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.170
Write the rule down, publish the

53
00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.630
scores, and let people check them.

54
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.810
In the app, give each class one teacher.

55
00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.010
Compare first come, first

56
00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.970
served with the best total.

57
00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.140
Then change Karim’s scores,

58
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.960
and see who loses out.

59
00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:38.640
Your turn.

60
00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.650
A rota has the best total, but one

61
00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:45.470
teacher gets the worst duty every week.

62
00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.980
What do you change in the model?

63
00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:52.160
Add a floor for everyone, then make

64
00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.260
the total as big as possible.

65
00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.840
Remember: the total, the worst-off and

66
00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.920
the gap measure different things.

67
00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.110
Fairness goes into the model

68
00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.770
as limits or goals.

69
00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.610
And agree the rule with the people

70
00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.510
affected, then publish it.

71
00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.140
Try it in class tomorrow: give groups

72
00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.480
a small table of how much three

73
00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.460
pupils like three class jobs.

74
00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.020
One group finds the best total;

75
00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.060
another makes the least happy

76
00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.960
pupil as happy as possible.

77
00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.740
Compare: what did fairness cost, and

78
00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.400
which plan would the class choose?
